nodecode-anyapi is a rewrite of es697's es697/hermes-provider-anyapi:
https://github.com/es697/hermes-provider-anyapi
commit e5b7b985b5aa56bc585ef1924858978696eb0c3a
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AnyAPI (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the provider profile (its base, its key variable, the
catalog row it becomes), the reading of AnyAPI's catalog `tags` that keeps
only the routes accepting tool calls, the fallback to the unfiltered listing
when that read fails or names none, the cache that keeps one answered
catalog for the process, the fallback model roster, and the deferral to the
generic listing when the base is not AnyAPI's own. The profile became a
config section (`base_url`, `tool_capable`, `timeout_seconds`) plus three
hooks: the catalog row, the credential and the model listing. The Hermes
plumbing the plugin relied on rather than wrote -- the model picker, `/model`,
`doctor`, `--provider`, the credential resolution -- is the core's here and
was not rewritten. The provider id is `anyapi` rather than `anyapi.ai`, which
is what makes the core's own `<ID>_API_KEY` ladder read `ANYAPI_API_KEY`.

What was left out: the profile fields Nodecode has no use for (the `any-api`
alias, `hostname`, `auth_type`, `api_mode`, `signup_url` as profile data,
`supports_vision` as a profile-wide claim, and `default_aux_model`, which
Nodecode pins per session in its own config), and `ANYAPI_BASE_URL`, whose
place the section's `base_url` takes. A key `/connect` saves answers as it
does for any other provider, without code here: the plugin's registry did
that for it, and so does the core.
